n the community is  evolving it's a great achievement i mean  it's a sign of the times in terms of  change  we are a conservative community by  nature and  take this step forward i think is large  deer isn't new to politics having served  12 years  as a council chief she wasn't available  for interviews  sunday but on saturday she said one of  her priorities  would be looking at governance finding a  way to return to  governing structure you know that's more  reflective of who we are  as first nations people she underscored  the need for governments to do  more to support hers and other first  nations communities  this isn't a handout this is what's owed  to us and it's a drop in the bucket  compared to what we should be getting  another priority to help guide the  community through the trauma  of residential schools our community  right now  is in a very sad state with all of the  you know recent discoveries of these  children across turtle island  and that you know right now what we need  is uh  is healing her father who observes  traditional rituals says his daughter  follows in his footsteps  she speaks the language for instance he  believes she is well placed to  not only help unite her village but to  help build bridges  between it and the outside communities  my advice to my daughter  would be to never  come from a place of fear ever sky deer  steps into her new role as grand  chief monday phil carpenter global news  ganaway still ahead did you feel sick  after your kova 19 shots  we look into the different reactions  more than 34 percent of eligible  canadians are now fully vaccinated  and some people have experienced side  effects others have felt nothing at all  so does the lack of reaction mean less  protection our health reporter jamie  morocco  is looking into this tonight  for months amanda ferguson who is  immunocompromised has been part of a  study out of toronto sinai health  monitoring her covid19 antibody levels  post vaccine  i wanted that sign that my body and my  immune system was working  and other than a little bit of fatigue i  didn't really feel much  living with crohn's that lack of  symptoms after her first pfizer shot had  her worried she wasn't building immunity  but her results gave her good news 16  days roughly past the first shot then  you saw  oh my gosh i'm protected doctors say  reactions to the covet-19 vaccines range  some people feel slight soreness at the  injection site others suffer from muscle  aches headaches and fever  i don't think that people who haven't  had this really robust  reaction after vaccine are  need to be concerned at all and while  most experts agree earl brown a  professor of virology at the university  of ottawa notes  immunity is linked to inflammation the  vaccine has to stimulate inflammation  that your body  responds to so you don't have to feel  unwell  but you have to have an activated immune  system from your vaccine  brown also points out different vaccines  can prompt different reactions  it is a dance when you're vaccinating  getting  a vaccine which will stimulate your  immune response  sufficiently but not excessively after  her second dose of pfizer ferguson says  she was left with a sore arm  and more anxiety as she awaited her  levels the results came back loud and  clear that not only like i had a good  amount after the first shot but then i  had a really good number after the  second  peace of mind she says and proof the  size of the reaction  doesn't equal the amount of protection  jamie morocco global news toronto  up next this dog knows how to heal we'll  tell you about the four-legged therapy  for hospital staff  a k-9 companion in calgary is scoring  points with hospital staff  tucker has been boosting the spirits of  those working on the front lines during  one of the most stressful times  in history here's lauren pullen on the  free form of therapy  that's working wonders in emergency  rooms from coast to coast  doctors expect the unexpected but this  was different  we were not only at war with this  coveted virus in the emergency  department  but we as healthcare workers could be  the casualties  a front-line fight with stress like  never before  we lost a lot of sleep not knowing what  was going to happen  we never knew what was around the corner  for health care workers and those  needing critical care during the  pandemic  there are days that are simply  overwhelming but just when it all seems  to be too much  it's kind of like having a movie star  walk in  it's it's magic some unconditional love  when it's needed the most tucker was my  retirement president  he's my best friend larry gertzen wanted  to share some of that four-legged  affection so for the past four years the  pair has volunteered at one of calgary's  busiest hospitals  and now everyone knows tucker by name  armed with his own official badge the  seven-year-old english lab roams the  hospital halls  gladly greeting healthcare workers and  visiting patients for some quality  time and stress relief just a way for  you know for us to kind of escape  even if it's for the five minutes of  getting a pet in with  with tucker let's go quick quick  tucker is the high point of my week  during the height of the pandemic the  hospital had to press pause on the  visits but it was one of the first  volunteer programs brought back when it  was safe  and for good reason canadian research  shows that patients  across the board feel better when the  dog is around  both even the pain level seemed to  moderate just by having the dog  there and even for larry it's just a  good feeling  and i know it helps me  a little compassion care and even a  keepsake  and of course we give them a trading  card and i go through a lot of these  and in a time and place where smiles  aren't always easy to come by  that little bit of tucker tlc makes all  the difference  good boy are you a good boy  yeah lauren pulling global news calgary  what a sweet story that is global  national for this sunday night i'm robin  gill  tonight your canada is deep cove in  north vancouver we'd love to see your  corner of the country so please keep  sending your photos  to viewers at globalnational.com thank  you for watching  and i'll see you next weekend have a  great night  [Music]  you
 

